---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Download – ContestLogX">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center px-5 py-10">

    <div class="max-w-4xl w-full text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">Download ContestLogX</h1>

      <p class="text-lg opacity-80 mb-12">
        ContestLogX is currently in beta. Download the latest version for your platform below.
      </p>

      <!-- Download sections -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
        <div class="rounded-lg border p-8" style="background-color: #161b22; border-color: #30363d;">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Linux</h2>
          <p class="mb-2 opacity-80">Version 0.9.3 (Beta)</p>
          <p class="mb-6 opacity-60 text-sm">AppImage · tar.gz</p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/sjwoodr/ContestLogX/releases/download/v0.9.3/ContestLogX.0.9.3.AppImage.tar.gz"
            class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold transition-colors download-btn"
          >
            Download for Linux
          </a>
          <style>
            .download-btn {
              background-color: #238636;
              color: #ffffff;
            }
            .download-btn:hover {
              background-color: #2ea043;
            }
          </style>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg border p-8" style="background-color: #161b22; border-color: #30363d;">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">macOS</h2>
          <p class="mb-2 opacity-80">Version 0.9.3 (Beta)</p>
          <p class="mb-6 opacity-60 text-sm">App Bundle · tar.gz</p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/sjwoodr/ContestLogX/releases/download/v0.9.3/ContestLogX.0.9.3.macOS.tar.gz"
            class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold transition-colors download-btn"
          >
            Download for macOS
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-lg border p-8" style="background-color: #161b22; border-color: #30363d;">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Windows</h2>
          <p class="mb-2 opacity-80">Version 0.9.3 (Beta)</p>
          <p class="mb-6 opacity-60 text-sm">Portable · self-extracting exe</p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/sjwoodr/ContestLogX/releases/download/v0.9.3/ContestLogX.0.9.3.Windows.exe"
            class="inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold transition-colors download-btn"
          >
            Download for Windows
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- macOS first-launch instructions -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border p-8 text-left mb-8" style="background-color: #161b22; border-color: #30363d;">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">First launch on macOS</h2>
        <p class="opacity-80 mb-4">
          ContestLogX for macOS is signed ad-hoc (not notarized by Apple), so on first launch
          Gatekeeper will block it with the message
          <em>"ContestLogX.app was blocked to protect your Mac."</em>
          This is expected. Choose either option below to unlock the app:
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Option A &mdash; Via System Settings (recommended for most users)</h3>
        <ol class="space-y-1 opacity-80 list-decimal pl-6 mb-4">
          <li>Double-click <code>ContestLogX.app</code> once. macOS will show a warning dialog; click <strong>Done</strong>.</li>
          <li>Open <strong>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security</strong>.</li>
          <li>Scroll down to the <strong>Security</strong> section. You will see
              <em>"ContestLogX.app was blocked to protect your Mac."</em> with an
              <strong>Open Anyway</strong> button &mdash; click it.</li>
          <li>Authenticate with Touch ID or your password. The app will launch and is trusted from now on.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Option B &mdash; Via Terminal (one command)</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80 mb-2">
          After dragging <code>ContestLogX.app</code> into <code>/Applications</code>, open
          <strong>Terminal</strong> and run:
        </p>
        <pre class="rounded-md p-3 mb-2" style="background-color: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; overflow-x: auto;"><code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/ContestLogX.app</code></pre>
        <p class="opacity-80 mb-4">
          This removes the download-quarantine flag macOS sets on files from the internet.
          After that, double-click normally to launch.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Microphone access (CW Decoder)</h3>
        <p class="opacity-80">
          When you first enable the CW Decoder and select an audio input device,
          macOS will ask permission to use the microphone &mdash; click <strong>Allow</strong>.
          Without this, the decoder will receive a silent stream and produce no output.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- System Requirements -->
      <div class="bg-[--color-gh-card] rounded-lg border border-[--color-gh-border] p-8 text-left">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">System Requirements</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 opacity-80">
          <li><strong>Operating System:</strong> Linux (glibc 2.35+ &mdash; Ubuntu 22.04+, Fedora 36+, or equivalent), macOS 11.0 Big Sur or later (Intel or Apple Silicon), or Windows 10+</li>
          <li><strong>Memory:</strong> 1 GB RAM minimum, 2 GB recommended</li>
          <li><strong>Storage:</strong> 100 MB available space</li>
          <li><strong>Display:</strong> 1024x768 minimum resolution</li>
          <li><strong>Optional:</strong> <a href="https://www.w1hkj.org/" class="underline" style="color: #58a6ff;">flrig</a> for rig control</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
